<p style="font-size:11px;color:#666;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;margin-top:6px;">WTI crude has fallen nearly six per cent from its August 21 close as reports of Iran-Oman talks on a temporary Strait of Hormuz maritime corridor eased supply concern. Source: Investing.com futures data.</p>
<p>USD/CAD has climbed back most of the way toward its August high over the same six trading days that WTI fell nearly six per cent in the opposite direction, a divergence in magnitude that the currency’s usual energy correlation does not explain on its own.</p>
